      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "C. difficile: fidaxomicin (preferred by IDSA/SHEA; less recurrence than vancomycin) or oral vancomycin for 10 days; oral metronidazole only if neither is available. Fulminant without ileus: vancomycin 500 mg orally 4 times a day + metronidazole 500 mg IV every 8 hours."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Cholera: doxycycline is first-line for nonpregnant adults; azithromycin is first-line for children and pregnant women and second-line for others."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Giardiasis: tinidazole (single dose), metronidazole (5-7 days), secnidazole (single dose) or nitazoxanide (3 days; liquid form for children)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Amebiasis: metronidazole 7-10 days or tinidazole (secnidazole, ornidazole), avoiding alcohol; then iodoquinol for 20 days or paromomycin for 7 days (safe in pregnancy) to clear cysts."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Diphenoxylate/atropine is the other effective antidiarrheal; antimotility drugs aren't recommended in children < 18 years with acute diarrhea."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
